    %% Several staff actor FKs share one line per table pair:
    %% staff_assignments.assigned_by_staff_id and removed_by_staff_id;
    %% blood_units.started_by_staff_id, completed_by_staff_id,
    %% separated_by_staff_id; requests.submitted_by_staff_id and
    %% accepted_by_staff_id and rejected_by_staff_id. No extra staff line is drawn for those pairs.
    %% donations.status: Pending, assessment_deferred, Eligible,
    %% Collecting, Collected, collection_failed, quarantine,
    %% separation_failed, Finalized, or lab_failed.
    %% assessment_results.final_decision: Eligible or Deferred.
    %% assessment_results.deferral_type: temporary or permanent when Deferred.
    %% Temporary deferral requires deferral_until; permanent deferral does not.
    %% Eligible decisions have no deferral fields.
    %% blood_units.collection_status: Collecting, Collected, or Failed.
    %% A failed collection may have no bag_reference or quarantined_at.
    %% blood_units.separation_outcome: Successful or Failed.
    %% lab_test_results.status: Passed or Failed.
    %% Failed tests may require follow-up with a recorded reason.
    %% blood_components.status: Awaiting_tests, Available, allocated,
    %% marked_for_disposal, or disposed.
    %% Copy verified ABO/Rh from the lab result to separated components
    %% when it becomes available; do not treat empty values as cleared stock.
    %% Component release requires successful separation, accepted
    %% processing, a Passed lab result, verified ABO/Rh, and no expiry.
    %% blood_components.donation_id must match its blood unit's donation_id.
    %% requests.patient_reference is scoped to its hospital_id.
    %% staff_assignments.scope must agree with roles.scope: system roles
    %% have no organization, bank roles one blood bank, and hospital roles
    %% one hospital. Removed assignments no longer grant access.
    %% Request acceptance allocates the full exact-match quantity
    %% from one bank in a single transaction.

    %% Requirement reconciliation, 27 October 2026:
    %% Every submitted request retains one addressed_bank_id and the submission match snapshot.
    %% accepted_bank_id keeps its original meaning and must equal addressed_bank_id when accepted.
    %% Match searches are transient; no-match/cancelled searches create no submitted request.
    %% component_type, ABO/Rh and the full quantity must match current available stock at one nearest bank.
    %% Once submitted, addressed bank, submitted_at, component/group and quantity remain original facts.
    %% Request editing/rerouting/correction policies are not introduced by this revision.
    %% Only pending requests may be decided. Accepted requests have acceptance actor/time and no rejection fields.
    %% Rejected requests have rejected_at, rejection_source and rejection_reason; manual rejection also requires an actor.
    %% Automatic rejection has rejection_source=automatic and rejected_by_staff_id=null, never a fabricated staff account.
    %% Pending requests have neither acceptance nor rejection audit values.
    %% Acceptance rechecks stock and reserves exactly quantity_units atomically; no partial reservations.
    %% In that decision transaction, reevaluate similar pending requests at the addressed bank;
    %% reject insufficient requests automatically and leave sufficiently supplied requests pending.
    %% Pending-request and expiry notices are bank-scoped read projections of these durable records.
    %% Expiry notices select expired, undisposed components; request notices select pending addressed requests.
    %% No notice/read-receipt table or external messaging provider is implied; delivery history is not required here.
    %% is_available must check current expiry even if the expiry-monitor task or notice publication fails.
    %% Forecast runs belong to one bank; component/group series are identified in result_manifest and point fields.
    %% Forecast bank attribution uses addressed_bank_id at submitted_at, including later rejected requests.
    %% Historical attribution requires reliable evidence; accepted_bank_id or today's nearest bank is not a substitute.
    %% Each run freezes its cutoff, original submission snapshot, completeness, versions and artifact references.
    %% Forecast snapshots contain authorized aggregates, not patient references, donor records or credentials.
    %% forecast_runs.status: queued, running, succeeded, partial, or failed.
    %% Unique forecast run key: (blood_bank_id, requested_by_staff_id, idempotency_key).
    %% An existing idempotency key with a different input_fingerprint is a conflict, not a new run.
    %% Unique demand point key: (forecast_run_id, component_type, abo_group, rh_factor, forecast_date).
    %% A daily point has finite nonnegative predicted_units: expected new submitted-request units, not stock.
    %% result_status is ok or fallback. Unavailable series have no fabricated zero points;
    %% their status/reason is retained in result_manifest, including runs with no successful points.
    %% Optional p10/p50/p90 are all null unless validated; otherwise require nonnegative ordered quantiles.
    %% Published succeeded/partial results and their provenance are immutable. Regeneration creates a new run.
    %% A queued/running/failed run may have zero points; no failed run is presented as a saved successful forecast.
    %% FR-22 retrieves the selected saved result without recomputation or substitution.
    %% Forecast generation never reserves inventory or changes request decisions.
    %% Offline synchronization remains a separate architecture design; completeness watermarks do not implement sync.
    %% Snapshot-dependent fields may be null while queued/preparing or when preparation fails.
    %% Succeeded/partial publication requires complete dataset/snapshot identifiers, checksums,
    %% actual history window and completeness watermark. Never use placeholder provenance values.
